  "issue_evidence": {
    "issue_number": 714,
    "repository": "swiftlang/swift-format",
    "title": "NoAccessLevelOnExtensionDeclaration should move @_spi attribute with access level attribute",
    "state": "closed",
    "status_reason": "completed",
    "body": "If an extension is marked with an access level attribute and has the @_spi attribute, the NoAccessLevelOnExtensionDeclaration rule should move both attributes to each declaration in the extension.\n\nfunc testExtensionWithSpiAttribute() {\n  assertFormatting(\n    NoAccessLevelOnExtensionDeclaration.self,\n    input: \"\"\"\n      @_spi(Something) public extension Foo {\n        var bar: String { \"\" }\n      }\n      \"\"\",\n    expected: \"\"\"\n      extension Foo {\n        @_spi(Something) public var bar: String { \"\" }\n      }\n      \"\"\",\n    findings: [\n      // TODO: Add findings\n    ]\n  )\n}\n\nOriginated from: swiftlang/swift-syntax#2602 (comment)",
    "issue_type": "bug_report_with_reproducer",
    "fix_commit": "a1e240991cae3e0974c803486fe01ea85aa713f9",
    "fix_message": "fixes #714: move @_spi with access level"
  },
  "dataset_id": "SWIFT-D034",
  "patch_sha256": "51aee43b412c08947e28fd51b4933a66814abccb2d53b8e58630db62ce2a2485",
  "revision_alias_semantics": "buggy_commit/fixed_commit identify upstream provenance; experimental b/f identities are in artifacts",
  "upstream_fix": {
    "commit": "a1e240991cae3e0974c803486fe01ea85aa713f9",
    "parents": [
      "38f6e71de1152862dad2ea76760abc43aaa18ac2"
    ],
    "buggy_baseline_is_parent": true,
    "single_parent_matches_baseline": true,
    "commit_message": "Move @_spi attributes to members in NoAccessLevelOnExtensionDeclaration\n\nWhen NoAccessLevelOnExtensionDeclaration moves an explicit access level\nfrom an extension down to its members, it left any @_spi attribute behind\non the extension. An @_spi attribute on an extension only takes effect\nwhen the extension also carries an explicit access level, and it applies\nto the members the same way that access level does. Stripping the access\nlevel while leaving @_spi on the extension is inconsistent with the rule's\npurpose of pushing member-affecting modifiers down to each member.\n\nThe rule now collects @_spi attributes from the extension and prepends\nthem to each member alongside the access level, so\n\n    @_spi(Something) public extension Foo {\n      var bar: String { \"\" }\n    }\n\nbecomes\n\n    extension Foo {\n      @_spi(Something) public var bar: String { \"\" }\n    }\n\nAttributes that genuinely belong on the extension, such as @objc and\n@available, are left untouched. When the access level is the redundant\ninternal keyword the members are not modified, so the @_spi attribute\nstays on the extension as before.\n\nFixes #714.",
